---
args: { input: CaseInput }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind `goal = await frameRequest(input)` from the request and `policy = await selectPolicy(input)` from supplied authority candidates. Preserve unresolved precedence instead of guessing which source governs.
2. Bind `work = await formTaskGraph(goal)` and `evidencePlan = await planEvidence(input, work)` so each operation has explicit prerequisites and a searched source universe.
3. Run the stages in their dependency order. The first stage receives only `input.domainRecords.firstStage`; every later stage receives the preceding function's actual accepted records. Bind each full result separately.
const constructCandidatesResult = await constructCandidates(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan);
const judgePairsResult = await judgePairs(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, constructCandidatesResult.accepted);
const reconcileClustersResult = await reconcileClusters(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, judgePairsResult.accepted);
const constructCanonicalResult = await constructCanonical(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, reconcileClustersResult.accepted);
const maintainIdentityResult = await maintainIdentity(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, constructCanonicalResult.accepted);
4. Bind `stageSet: CaseStageSet = { constructCandidates: constructCandidatesResult, judgePairs: judgePairsResult, reconcileClusters: reconcileClustersResult, constructCanonical: constructCanonicalResult, maintainIdentity: maintainIdentityResult }` and `collection: CollectionFinding = await reconcileCollection(stageSet)`. Bind `allQuestions: string[] = [...constructCandidatesResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...judgePairsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...reconcileClustersResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...constructCanonicalResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...maintainIdentityResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...collection.coverageGaps]` and `questions: QuestionBatch = await resolveQuestions(allQuestions, input)`.
5. Bind `invalidation = await assessDelta(input)`, `review = await prepareReview(collection)`, and `view = await composeView(review, input)`; pass each child its actual declared inputs and retain the returned object.
6. Bind `allChecks: CheckResult[] = [...constructCandidatesResult.checks, ...judgePairsResult.checks, ...reconcileClustersResult.checks, ...constructCanonicalResult.checks, ...maintainIdentityResult.checks]`. Bind `hasGateFailure = allChecks.some(check => check.verdict !== "pass")` and `hasBlocker = input.authorityStatus !== "authorized" || questions.questions.length > 0 || collection.coverageGaps.length > 0`. Bind `disposition: "proposed" | "blocked" | "needs-review" = hasBlocker ? "blocked" : hasGateFailure ? "needs-review" : "proposed"`. Bind `rationale: string[] = allChecks.map(check => `${check.check}: ${check.verdict}; evidence ${check.evidenceIds.join(",")}`)`.
7. Operational detail 1 — A parent and subsidiary share an address: represent their relationship without merging identities. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (represent their relationship without merging identities.) through the existing stage result for IdentityCandidate; preserve exact source/version and the prior IdentityCandidate, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
8. Operational detail 2 — Two people share a name and employer: require stronger evidence before linking. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (require stronger evidence before linking.) through the existing stage result for IdentityCandidate; preserve exact source/version and the prior IdentityCandidate, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
9. Operational detail 3 — A merge is later reversed: propagate the split to dependent records and preserve audit history. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (propagate the split to dependent records and preserve audit history.) through the existing stage result for IdentityCandidate; preserve exact source/version and the prior IdentityCandidate, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
10. Operational detail 4 — A record has a recycled identifier: bind identity to its validity interval. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (bind identity to its validity interval.) through the existing stage result for IdentityCandidate; preserve exact source/version and the prior IdentityCandidate, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
11. Operational detail 5 — A source is revoked: remove its contribution from canonical values and reassess dependent links. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (remove its contribution from canonical values and reassess dependent links.) through the existing stage result for IdentityCandidate; preserve exact source/version and the prior IdentityCandidate, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
12. Initialize `revisions: RevisionProposal[] = []`. If any gate is not pass, bind `revision = await proposeRevision(the failed check names, the smallest affected stage name)` and add that returned proposal to revisions. Bind and return `result: RunProposal = { caseId: input.caseId, goal, policy, work, evidencePlan, constructCandidates: constructCandidatesResult, judgePairs: judgePairsResult, reconcileClusters: reconcileClustersResult, constructCanonical: constructCanonicalResult, maintainIdentity: maintainIdentityResult, collection, questions, invalidation, review, view, revisions, disposition, rationale }`. Proposed actions remain proposals. The host owns authorization, persistence, effect dispatch and verification.
